<title>USA: FSA qualifies six muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies six muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Thursday it qualified for bond insurance the following six municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Concord Community Schools, Ind., $4.7 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Cambridge ISD, Minn., $18.72 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Barnard, N.Y., $2.2 million Fire Department GOs.</p>
<p>--Plattsburgh, N.Y., $3.65 million various purpose bonds.</p>
<p>--Harris County Municipal Utility District No 46, Texas, $1.16 million water and sewer bonds.</p>
<p>--Delavan, Wis., $1.2 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
